Chapter: BoundedBudgetedShow
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The guard on `show`'s registry row, and the reason it exists is that nothing
 else in the tree can observe that row. `show` dispatches on its ARGUMENT'S
 TYPE and one path is `__itoa`, the helper `integer-to-text` declares
 `budgeted`, so a per-name class cannot describe it and the row reads
 `unknown`. A `bounded budgeted` ceiling over a body calling `show` must
 therefore be REFUSED. This arm COMPILES, when it should be refused, if the
 row is ever loosened back to `fixed`: it compiled up to 2026-09-07.

Section: The Declaration That Cannot Hold

  bounded budgeted labels : Integer -> Text
  labels (n) = show n

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (labels 7)
  end
